# Job Application Templates

Reference for tailoring resumes and writing cover letters. Read alongside [profile.md](profile.md), [master-resume.md](master-resume.md), and [Resume-Master.pdf](Resume-Master.pdf).

Applicant file prefix (from `config.json`): **{{file_prefix}}**

---

## Master Resume Style

**Always follow this layout.** Tailored resumes must match the master PDF format — only content changes per role.

Canonical reference: [Resume-Master.pdf](Resume-Master.pdf)

### Header

```
{{full_name}}
{{contact_line}}
```

- Name on line 1; contact details on line 2, pipe-separated
- Include portfolio / GitHub URLs from config; do **not** add a separate location line
- Plain text URLs — no markdown links, no bold

### Section Order

1. SUMMARY
2. EXPERIENCE
3. PROJECTS
4. SKILLS
5. EDUCATION

### Section Headings

- ALL CAPS: `## SUMMARY`, `## EXPERIENCE`, `## PROJECTS`, `## SKILLS`, `## EDUCATION`
- No horizontal rules (`---`) between sections
- No bold subheadings within sections

### Summary

- One prose paragraph (4–5 sentences)
- Professional and confident yet humble
- End with role intent aligned to the listing

### Experience

```
Role Title
Organisation City Country

- [purpose + outcome bullet]
- [bullet]
```

- Role title on its own line
- Organisation on the next line
- Blank line after organisation, before bullets
- Dash bullets (`-`)
- Blank line between each experience entry
- Only include roles evidenced in `profile.md`

### Resume bullet quality (purpose + outcome)

Every experience and project bullet must state **why the work mattered** or **what changed**, not only what you did.

| Element | Question |
| -------- | -------- |
| **Action** | What did you do? |
| **Purpose** | What problem did it solve or why was it needed? |
| **Outcome** | What improved for users, the team, or quality? |

**Avoid activity-only bullets.** Check `profile.md` "Claims to Avoid" before writing.

### Projects

```
Project Name — Description (Solo|Team of N)
Tech, Stack, Comma, Separated
github.com/you/repo-name

- [bullet]
- [bullet]
```

- Em dash (`—`) in title; optional team context in parentheses
- Tech stack plain comma-separated
- GitHub URL plain text (no `https://`, no markdown links)
- 3–5 bullets; reorder by relevance to the listing

### Skills

Flat category lines — no bold labels, no bullet lists:

```
Languages: …
Backend: …
Frontend: …
Databases: …
Testing & Tools: …
```

Only list skills with evidence in `profile.md`.

### Education

```
Degree Title
Institution • Country • Year
```

### What Not to Do

- No markdown links (`[text](url)`)
- No bold/italic formatting in body content
- No `---` horizontal rules
- No separate location line in the header
- No extra sections unless the user asks
- Never invent experience

