## Tailoring Checklist

```
- [ ] Read listing — required skills, nice-to-haves, company values, role level
- [ ] Read profile.md, master-resume.md, and Resume-Master.pdf
- [ ] Select 2–3 most relevant projects (reorder; do not invent)
- [ ] Work auth: {{work_auth_note}}
- [ ] Rewrite summary to mirror listing language (without keyword stuffing)
- [ ] Adjust skills order to match listing priorities
- [ ] Purpose/outcome pass on every bullet
- [ ] Format pass — match Master Resume Style
- [ ] Export PDFs: python3 scripts/export_application_pdfs.py {slug}
- [ ] Write cover letter (if requested)
- [ ] Spelling pass ({{spelling}})
- [ ] Tone pass
- [ ] Save using Output File Naming below
```

---

## Cover Letter Template

**Length:** 300–400 words  
**Tone:** Professional and friendly. Confident about demonstrated skills; humble about growth.

```markdown
Dear [Hiring Manager / Hiring Team / name],

[Paragraph 1 — Hook + role]
I am writing to apply for the [Role Title] position at [Company]. …

[Paragraph 2 — Relevant technical experience]
…

[Paragraph 3 — Team / soft skills + growth mindset]
…

[Paragraph 4 — Close]
…

Kind regards,
{{full_name}}
{{phone}}
{{email}}
```

### Cover Letter Rules

1. Use user-provided motivation when given
2. Do not fabricate company knowledge
3. Mirror listing language naturally
4. One project deep-dive beats listing every project
5. Avoid clichés ("passionate", "hit the ground running", "perfect fit")
6. Spelling: {{spelling}}

---

## Output File Naming

Save under `applications/{company}-{role-slug}/`:

| Document | Filename |
|----------|----------|
| Resume | `{{file_prefix}}-Resume-{Company Name}.md` |
| Cover letter | `{{file_prefix}}-CoverLetter-{Company Name}.md` |
| Notes | `notes.md` |

Use the company name as it appears in the listing.

---

## Updating the Workflow

| File | What to change |
|------|----------------|
| `config.json` | Name, file prefix, search market, schedule |
| `SKILL.md` | Workflow steps (re-run bootstrap after editing `.tmpl`) |
| `profile.md` | Skills, projects, preferences |
| `master-resume.md` | Base resume content |
| `Resume-Master.pdf` | Layout reference (regenerated by bootstrap) |
| `templates.md` | Style + cover letter rules |
